# NOTE: gitignore has no inline comments. A trailing "# ..." becomes part of
# the pattern, so the rule silently never matches. Every comment here is on its
# own line for that reason.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Node / build toolchain
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# The generated component bundle IS committed so `pip install -e .` works
# without a JS build. Only the build-time react-docgen artifact is excluded —
# it is ~27 MB and nothing loads it at runtime.
dash_leaflet2/metadata.json

# Secrets and local environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Runtime state written by the app.
# page_visibility.json — control-board overrides, per-deployment
# visitor_analytics.json — the 2plot.ai analytics ledger (plus its .lock/.tmp

# Flask-Session's server-side session store. dash-clerk-auth creates it in
# the CWD the moment Clerk is configured, so any local run WITH the CLERK_*
# keys drops session blobs into the repo — and `git add -A` will happily
# commit somebody's session token. Never tracked.
flask_session/
#   siblings and the reporter's lease file). Committing it would publish
#   visitor IPs and user agents.
# satellite_traffic.jsonl — the RETIRED Gen-1 ledger; kept ignored so a stale
#   local copy can never be committed.
page_visibility.json
visitor_analytics.json
visitor_analytics.json.*
.satellite_report.lease
satellite_traffic.jsonl
.satellite_traffic.jsonl.*

# Test harness scratch — scripts/compat_matrix.py venvs and raw results
.compat/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Session working documents are LOCAL BY CONVENTION, network-wide: sync
# reports, handoffs, and kickoff briefs name hosts, topology, and process.
# Two public fleet repos were caught tracking theirs and clerkhook's staged
# handoff (naming the full satellite inventory) was one push from public
# (2026-08-24). The ignore rule is the enforcement, here and in every fork.
# This repo carried X402-SYNC-REPORT.md in .git/info/exclude, which is
# LOCAL-ONLY — it protected this checkout and nobody else's clone.
X402-SYNC-REPORT.md
HANDOFF-*.md
KICKOFF-*.md

# The .claude/ development kit IS shipped — it is how every fork inherits
# the network's behavioral contract, skills, and settings (the F1 fabric
# build, 2026-08-24). Everything else in .claude/ stays local: session
# scratch, screenshots, settings.local.json (per-seat model overrides),
# vendored iteration copies. Allow-list, not blanket ignore — a dir-level
# ignore cannot be re-included beneath, hence the /* form. The blanket
# `.claude/` that used to sit here is why this repo's root CLAUDE.md
# advertised `.claude/rules/` and a `/new-component` skill that no clone
# has ever had: they live in the private R&D checkout and were ignored out
# of the mirror.
.claude/*
!.claude/CLAUDE.md
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/skills/
